00:00:20.022 --> 00:00:20.855
Enjoy.

00:00:21.856 --> 00:00:24.439
(upbeat music)

00:00:39.248 --> 00:00:41.844
- Have you ever got in
the middle of your day

00:00:41.844 --> 00:00:44.002
and things just fell apart
and you were just like

00:00:44.002 --> 00:00:45.419
I need a restart?

00:00:46.701 --> 00:00:49.076
You just wanted to start
the whole day over.

00:00:49.076 --> 00:00:51.251
You were thinking things
were kind of going good

00:00:51.251 --> 00:00:52.576
and now I got derailed.

00:00:52.576 --> 00:00:55.357
I got distracted, I
stopped doing what I was

00:00:55.357 --> 00:00:56.413
supposed to be doing.

00:00:56.413 --> 00:00:58.120
I had a bad interaction with somebody

00:00:58.120 --> 00:01:00.256
or a conflict and now
I feel bad about myself

00:01:00.256 --> 00:01:02.793
or about the day and you
just overall were frustrated

00:01:02.793 --> 00:01:06.351
with where you were at and you
were struggling to restart.

00:01:06.351 --> 00:01:08.157
A lot of people don't have
the resiliency to restart

00:01:08.157 --> 00:01:11.561
in the middle of the day and so they lose

00:01:11.561 --> 00:01:14.587
those last couple of hours
or the rest of the entire day

00:01:14.587 --> 00:01:17.783
to a bad mood, to bad
energy, to bad productivity

00:01:17.783 --> 00:01:20.018
to being ineffective and because of that

00:01:20.018 --> 00:01:23.127
it's costing us great amounts of progress

00:01:23.127 --> 00:01:25.033
in our own personal lives and frankly

00:01:25.033 --> 00:01:27.189
as a country, a nation an economy.

00:01:27.189 --> 00:01:28.760
We struggle with it a lot.

00:01:28.760 --> 00:01:30.359
People need to become more resilient.

00:01:30.359 --> 00:01:32.618
So what can you do?

00:01:32.618 --> 00:01:35.201
(gentle music)

00:01:37.067 --> 00:01:38.471
- We all want to be able
to change the way we feel.

00:01:38.471 --> 00:01:40.358
That's what I spend my life
showing people how to do

00:01:40.358 --> 00:01:41.191
and what most people
don't know is the emotion

00:01:41.191 --> 00:01:42.313
is created by motion.

00:01:42.313 --> 00:01:44.809
The way you move determines
the way you feel.

00:01:44.809 --> 00:01:46.986
You have 80 different
muscles in your face, 80.

00:01:46.986 --> 00:01:49.203
For most people this is the largest area

00:01:49.203 --> 00:01:50.562
of unemployment in the country.

00:01:50.562 --> 00:01:52.630
They use the face the same way.

00:01:52.630 --> 00:01:54.770
They feel the same emotions
over and over and over again.

00:01:54.770 --> 00:01:56.901
So what I was saying is I have this deal

00:01:56.901 --> 00:01:57.940
with myself called priming.

00:01:57.940 --> 00:02:00.622
Every day I say, look, you got to have

00:02:00.622 --> 00:02:01.614
10 minutes for yourself.

00:02:01.614 --> 00:02:03.141
If you don't have 10 minutes,
you don't have a life

00:02:03.141 --> 00:02:04.662
and I'm not going to hope I feel good.

00:02:04.662 --> 00:02:07.379
I just got back 6 countries in 12 days.

00:02:07.379 --> 00:02:08.482
I was in India two days ago.

00:02:08.482 --> 00:02:09.480
- [Interviewer] Wow.

00:02:09.480 --> 00:02:10.473
- I woke up here feeling like somebody

00:02:10.473 --> 00:02:12.040
ran me over with a truck.

00:02:12.040 --> 00:02:14.612
- But you got yourself psyched up and-

00:02:14.612 --> 00:02:16.307
- But the way I did it
is I do this process.

00:02:16.307 --> 00:02:18.013
It's 10 minutes, I put some music on

00:02:18.013 --> 00:02:19.517
and I do this massive
change in my breathing

00:02:19.517 --> 00:02:21.183
so it radically changes the way I feel

00:02:21.183 --> 00:02:23.252
and then I do this three-step process.

00:02:23.252 --> 00:02:25.084
First I do three minutes of gratitude.

00:02:25.084 --> 00:02:27.458
I think of three things
I'm really grateful for.

00:02:27.458 --> 00:02:29.652
I don't think of it over there, I feel it.

00:02:29.652 --> 00:02:32.233
And the reason is when you're grateful,

00:02:32.233 --> 00:02:33.617
you can't be worried,
you can't be fearful.

00:02:33.617 --> 00:02:36.517
When you're grateful, you can't be angry

00:02:36.517 --> 00:02:39.039
and anger and fear are what
screw people up the most.

00:02:39.039 --> 00:02:41.053
In their relationships, in
their life and their business.

00:02:41.053 --> 00:02:42.484
So I wire myself.

00:02:42.484 --> 00:02:45.112
I was saying to you that
most people want to be happy,

00:02:45.112 --> 00:02:47.446
but their habit is to
be worried or pissed off

00:02:47.446 --> 00:02:50.517
or frustrated or stressed
and so they've got a highway

00:02:50.517 --> 00:02:53.131
of stress and they've got
a dirt road to happiness.

00:02:53.131 --> 00:02:54.411
So I wire myself.

00:02:54.411 --> 00:02:56.366
I've got a highway to
gratitude, which changes

00:02:56.366 --> 00:02:58.596
all your emotions and then
I do a three-minute process

00:02:58.596 --> 00:03:00.650
kind of a prayer for my family and friends

00:03:00.650 --> 00:03:02.496
and then I do a three-minute
process of the things

00:03:02.496 --> 00:03:03.494
I want to accomplish.

00:03:03.494 --> 00:03:05.160
I see it as done and I feel it.

00:03:05.160 --> 00:03:06.159
I'm done in 10 minutes.

00:03:06.159 --> 00:03:08.045
Sometimes I go 20, but my deal is 10,

00:03:08.045 --> 00:03:09.653
so there's no excuse not to do it.

00:03:09.653 --> 00:03:10.909
- You know what I think that's a great way

00:03:10.909 --> 00:03:12.453
to kind of set the tone for the day.

00:03:12.453 --> 00:03:13.447
- It does.

00:03:13.447 --> 00:03:15.663
It changes, listen we've all
had times that you snapped

00:03:15.663 --> 00:03:17.836
at somebody and you felt
bad because it wasn't them,

00:03:17.836 --> 00:03:20.178
it was the state you're in, right?

00:03:20.178 --> 00:03:21.194
Well, there's no excuse for that.

00:03:21.194 --> 00:03:23.504
If you prime yourself,
you set yourself up.

00:03:23.504 --> 00:03:25.518
They've done studies
where they go to people

00:03:25.518 --> 00:03:27.774
and they have a man walk up to you and say

00:03:27.774 --> 00:03:29.576
could you hold this for me
and hands you a cup of coffee,

00:03:29.576 --> 00:03:31.631
it's an actor, and they
take it, he takes something

00:03:31.631 --> 00:03:33.117
out of his pocket, then he takes
it back and says thank you.

00:03:33.117 --> 00:03:35.712
A hundred people they
do it with ice coffee,

00:03:35.712 --> 00:03:37.808
a hundred people they
do it with hot coffee.

00:03:37.808 --> 00:03:40.244
45 minutes later, another actor comes by

00:03:40.244 --> 00:03:42.152
and says listen, we're
doing this little test.

00:03:42.152 --> 00:03:44.449
For $5, would you read
this three paragraphs

00:03:44.449 --> 00:03:46.301
and answer three questions?

00:03:46.301 --> 00:03:48.274
Most people say yes.

00:03:48.274 --> 00:03:49.267
It's a little story.

00:03:49.267 --> 00:03:50.281
The questions are about the character,

00:03:50.281 --> 00:03:52.152
what's the character like?

00:03:52.152 --> 00:03:53.818
80% of the people that got iced coffee

00:03:53.818 --> 00:03:55.914
say the person is cold and mean.

00:03:55.914 --> 00:03:58.857
81% of the people that got hot coffee

00:03:58.857 --> 00:04:02.009
say the person is warm and gentle or nice.

00:04:02.009 --> 00:04:05.480
That's how much we can be
primed by our environment.

00:04:05.480 --> 00:04:06.736
We think we're just
feeling what we're feeling,

00:04:06.736 --> 00:04:08.487
but our environment, if
we don't take control

00:04:08.487 --> 00:04:10.502
of our environment, it
takes control of us.

00:04:10.502 --> 00:04:12.976
- There's a ton of bad
days being an entrepreneur,

00:04:12.976 --> 00:04:15.337
not to mention 98% of
entrepreneur ventures

00:04:15.337 --> 00:04:16.330
are going to fail.

00:04:16.330 --> 00:04:18.472
So there's going to be a
really bad (censored) day

00:04:18.472 --> 00:04:19.482
in your future.

00:04:19.482 --> 00:04:23.315
You know, hopefully not
for you or any of you.

00:04:25.107 --> 00:04:28.926
For me, I don't, I think it's
a very personal question.

00:04:28.926 --> 00:04:30.349
I think it's how you're wired.

00:04:30.349 --> 00:04:34.436
I'm so all in entrepreneur,
I prefer the pain.

00:04:34.436 --> 00:04:36.020
I think one of the reasons
I love the jet so much

00:04:36.020 --> 00:04:39.649
is because they bring me so much pain.

00:04:39.649 --> 00:04:41.254
I love the climb.

00:04:41.254 --> 00:04:44.581
To me the setback is exciting.

00:04:44.581 --> 00:04:46.679
I love when something goes wrong.

00:04:46.679 --> 00:04:48.528
It's where I shine the most,

00:04:48.528 --> 00:04:50.882
but that's not for everybody, right?

00:04:50.882 --> 00:04:52.957
It can be very difficult
and when you start

00:04:52.957 --> 00:04:54.704
affecting your life and your loved ones

00:04:54.704 --> 00:04:57.508
and all the other things,
it can get real nasty.

00:04:57.508 --> 00:05:01.427
To me, the way I handle
things, even the few rare days

00:05:01.427 --> 00:05:04.741
when I really struggle,
I take a real step back

00:05:04.741 --> 00:05:06.771
and make pretend that somebody called me

00:05:06.771 --> 00:05:10.795
and told me that my mother
and daughter were killed.

00:05:10.795 --> 00:05:13.027
And I know that's very
dark and I apologize,

00:05:13.027 --> 00:05:15.123
but it's really what I do.

00:05:15.123 --> 00:05:18.417
I literally am able to at my
deepest most struggling moment

00:05:18.417 --> 00:05:21.764
within business take a
step back and remind myself

00:05:21.764 --> 00:05:24.635
that I can make a
drillion dollars tomorrow

00:05:24.635 --> 00:05:28.634
on Bit Coin and if something bad happened

00:05:28.634 --> 00:05:30.323
to the people I love the most,

00:05:30.323 --> 00:05:32.965
that it would mean nothing
and it very consistently

00:05:32.965 --> 00:05:34.965
rewires me very quickly.

00:05:36.513 --> 00:05:38.771
I just put business in perspective.

00:05:38.771 --> 00:05:42.164
At the end of the day,
you know, it's money.

00:05:42.164 --> 00:05:43.164
For me it's not really money.

00:05:43.164 --> 00:05:45.155
It's my legacy, so I get
hurt by it a little bit more,

00:05:45.155 --> 00:05:48.072
but, yeah, I put it in perspective.

00:05:50.658 --> 00:05:52.121
It's money and you know what?

00:05:52.121 --> 00:05:54.740
Up until I had a daughter,
even while I was married,

00:05:54.740 --> 00:05:57.970
up until when I had Misha four years ago,

00:05:57.970 --> 00:06:00.956
I secretly wanted to lose all my money.

00:06:00.956 --> 00:06:04.674
I had this weird, twisted, dark fantasy

00:06:04.674 --> 00:06:07.951
of losing everything just to rise again

00:06:07.951 --> 00:06:12.032
like a phoenix and remind (censored).

00:06:12.032 --> 00:06:12.865
WTOH.

00:06:13.942 --> 00:06:16.543
What's the opportunity here?

00:06:16.543 --> 00:06:17.721
So you're having a bad day, maybe you had

00:06:17.721 --> 00:06:19.283
a fight with someone.

00:06:19.283 --> 00:06:21.541
Maybe you lost a big sale.

00:06:21.541 --> 00:06:24.016
Maybe someone cut you off in traffic

00:06:24.016 --> 00:06:27.252
and then you didn't
get your favorite lunch

00:06:27.252 --> 00:06:30.318
and then you missed getting
into Soul Cycle class

00:06:30.318 --> 00:06:32.937
and then you had a
difficulty on the way home.

00:06:32.937 --> 00:06:34.991
So let's say that's happening.

00:06:34.991 --> 00:06:37.741
You simply run the WTOH question,

00:06:38.873 --> 00:06:40.663
which will allow you to pivot.

00:06:40.663 --> 00:06:44.093
WTOH, what's the opportunity here?

00:06:44.093 --> 00:06:46.636
See there's great power in a question

00:06:46.636 --> 00:06:51.024
and it allows your brain
to hunt for something good.

00:06:51.024 --> 00:06:53.137
How do you pivot?

00:06:53.137 --> 00:06:55.918
You ask yourself what's
the opportunity here.

00:06:55.918 --> 00:06:57.329
You have a fight with someone,

00:06:57.329 --> 00:07:00.167
let's say one of your family members.

00:07:00.167 --> 00:07:02.402
Say what's the opportunity here.

00:07:02.402 --> 00:07:05.282
Well, your brain then starts
to look for the opportunity,

00:07:05.282 --> 00:07:08.006
which is I can learn how
to communicate better

00:07:08.006 --> 00:07:10.912
or this is an opportunity
for me to show forgiveness

00:07:10.912 --> 00:07:13.089
and grow in my personal bravery.

00:07:13.089 --> 00:07:15.667
This is an opportunity
for me to understand

00:07:15.667 --> 00:07:17.476
my family member better.

00:07:17.476 --> 00:07:19.893
It's a great and powerful question.

00:07:19.893 --> 00:07:22.354
- If I need to reset, I realize
the day's all gone to crap,

00:07:22.354 --> 00:07:24.764
I will immediately stop everything.

00:07:24.764 --> 00:07:27.433
If the day's gone to crap,
don't stay in your inbox,

00:07:27.433 --> 00:07:30.620
don't keep doing the
same thing you're doing.

00:07:30.620 --> 00:07:32.890
Take a step away from it.

00:07:32.890 --> 00:07:36.106
Literally go outside, take a walk.

00:07:36.106 --> 00:07:37.556
My favorite resets, I have two of them.

00:07:37.556 --> 00:07:41.642
One, I go outside, I
take my phone, I put on

00:07:41.642 --> 00:07:44.284
my favorite playlist of
music and I don't think

00:07:44.284 --> 00:07:46.117
about anything at all.

00:07:47.006 --> 00:07:50.379
I just listen to music
and I walk for 20 minutes.

00:07:50.379 --> 00:07:53.467
When I come back to my desk or I come back

00:07:53.467 --> 00:07:55.598
to the house or I come
back to wherever I was,

00:07:55.598 --> 00:08:00.172
I sit down, I bust out my
journal and I write three things.

00:08:00.172 --> 00:08:03.435
Number one, I start writing
everything I'm grateful for

00:08:03.435 --> 00:08:05.675
because I'm trying to take
my mind off of the day.

00:08:05.675 --> 00:08:08.299
So that's why I listen to
the music with no thoughts,

00:08:08.299 --> 00:08:09.924
just listen to the lyrics of the music,

00:08:09.924 --> 00:08:11.730
breathing as I'm walking.

00:08:11.730 --> 00:08:14.150
Sit down, what am I grateful for?

00:08:14.150 --> 00:08:17.767
Second, what three things
must be accomplished today?

00:08:17.767 --> 00:08:18.778
Write those down.

00:08:18.778 --> 00:08:21.970
Third, what's my reward if I
accomplish those three things?

00:08:21.970 --> 00:08:24.222
And for me, my reward is social, so I say

00:08:24.222 --> 00:08:26.358
if I finish these three, soon as I finish

00:08:26.358 --> 00:08:28.348
these three things, I get
to call my best friend

00:08:28.348 --> 00:08:30.237
from school who I haven't seen in years.

00:08:30.237 --> 00:08:32.571
If I finish these three
things, I get to call my lady.

00:08:32.571 --> 00:08:35.292
If I finish these three
things, I get to get up,

00:08:35.292 --> 00:08:38.346
I get to go have some green
tea and some chocolate,

00:08:38.346 --> 00:08:40.656
whatever it is for you.

00:08:40.656 --> 00:08:41.660
You need to have that reward.

00:08:41.660 --> 00:08:44.538
I write those down and it re-engages you

00:08:44.538 --> 00:08:45.717
with the blessings of
life, re-engages what I

00:08:45.717 --> 00:08:50.088
need to accomplish and re-engages
me with a simple reward.

00:08:50.088 --> 00:08:52.402
That's my first favorite way to reset.

00:08:52.402 --> 00:08:56.079
My second favorite way
to reset is meditation.

00:08:56.079 --> 00:08:59.149
To just stop everything, close my eyes,

00:08:59.149 --> 00:09:01.579
do the release meditation technique.

00:09:01.579 --> 00:09:03.118
If you haven't learned that before,

00:09:03.118 --> 00:09:04.284
you can learn that from me on YouTube.

00:09:04.284 --> 00:09:06.394
Just type in my name and then
release meditation technique

00:09:06.394 --> 00:09:08.713
and I do that for 20 minutes.

00:09:08.713 --> 00:09:12.021
When I open up my eyes,
I stand, I stretch,

00:09:12.021 --> 00:09:14.781
I get some water, I come back and again

00:09:14.781 --> 00:09:15.882
I write those three things.

00:09:15.882 --> 00:09:17.589
One I'm grateful for, what three things

00:09:17.589 --> 00:09:19.214
must be accomplished today and ultimately

00:09:19.214 --> 00:09:21.881
what's my reward for doing this?

00:09:22.971 --> 00:09:24.764
That's a great way to reset.

00:09:24.764 --> 00:09:27.202
I would say another one is to get outside

00:09:27.202 --> 00:09:30.290
of your head, to stop
thinking it all has to be you

00:09:30.290 --> 00:09:33.640
accomplishing everything
for you and another great

00:09:33.640 --> 00:09:35.897
reset is to ask this simple question.

00:09:35.897 --> 00:09:40.264
What could I do right
now to give a surprise,

00:09:40.264 --> 00:09:43.676
some attention or some
gratitude and appreciation

00:09:43.676 --> 00:09:45.509
to somebody around me?

00:09:46.602 --> 00:09:49.122
Could I go thank the receptionist,

00:09:49.122 --> 00:09:50.892
someone I haven't talked to in a while.

00:09:50.892 --> 00:09:53.302
Can I go pull a prank
on a friend over here?

00:09:53.302 --> 00:09:55.443
Can I call somebody
and prank them and make

00:09:55.443 --> 00:09:56.662
a joke with them?

00:09:56.662 --> 00:10:00.052
Can I call somebody
randomly and say thank you.

00:10:00.052 --> 00:10:02.432
Can I sit down and just
write a random thank you

00:10:02.432 --> 00:10:04.098
email to somebody I haven't
talked to in a while.

00:10:04.098 --> 00:10:05.805
Can I shoot and iPhone video sending love

00:10:05.805 --> 00:10:07.651
to family or a friend?

00:10:07.651 --> 00:10:11.186
Get outside of myself and
in service or surprise

00:10:11.186 --> 00:10:13.810
to somebody else helps me reboot the day

00:10:13.810 --> 00:10:16.794
because it gives me a social
enthusiasm to engage with

00:10:16.794 --> 00:10:17.877
with the day.

00:10:18.948 --> 00:10:21.548
As I was growing up as a
child, I would be quite

00:10:21.548 --> 00:10:23.640
envious of everybody else around me

00:10:23.640 --> 00:10:25.226
who had arms and legs,
including my brother

00:10:25.226 --> 00:10:26.587
and sister at times.

00:10:26.587 --> 00:10:29.066
I was born without limbs
for no medical reason.

00:10:29.066 --> 00:10:30.674
There are times in life
where things happen

00:10:30.674 --> 00:10:33.437
and don't make sense and I
was just sitting on a plane

00:10:33.437 --> 00:10:36.908
seat next to this guy who
was going to visit his mum

00:10:36.908 --> 00:10:39.509
and his stepfather just died on Friday,

00:10:39.509 --> 00:10:41.193
they're burying him
tomorrow or the day after

00:10:41.193 --> 00:10:43.247
and, you know, I was talking
with him a little bit

00:10:43.247 --> 00:10:44.466
and, you know, there are just some things

00:10:44.466 --> 00:10:47.148
that we won't understand in this life.

00:10:47.148 --> 00:10:48.489
Though there are some times when you wish

00:10:48.489 --> 00:10:52.535
that you could rewind and
do things all over again.

00:10:52.535 --> 00:10:55.555
There are times where you
just wish you could forget

00:10:55.555 --> 00:10:58.485
memories and you try to drown
those memories in alcohol

00:10:58.485 --> 00:11:00.517
or different pleasures
and maybe get distracted

00:11:00.517 --> 00:11:03.036
by the goals and ambitions
of your life and try to

00:11:03.036 --> 00:11:06.432
put the past behind and move forward.

00:11:06.432 --> 00:11:08.478
We're all human beings.

00:11:08.478 --> 00:11:09.548
Please don't get me wrong.

00:11:09.548 --> 00:11:11.462
I don't wake up every morning
with a smile on my face

00:11:11.462 --> 00:11:13.045
like, hi everybody.

00:11:15.201 --> 00:11:16.256
I have ups and downs.

00:11:16.256 --> 00:11:17.256
You see my foot?

00:11:17.256 --> 00:11:18.248
Ups and downs.

00:11:18.248 --> 00:11:19.261
Ups and downs.

00:11:19.261 --> 00:11:20.506
(laughing)

00:11:20.506 --> 00:11:21.888
The first thing I want you to take away

00:11:21.888 --> 00:11:23.717
from today is this.

00:11:23.717 --> 00:11:25.966
You will have good days
and you'll have bad days,

00:11:25.966 --> 00:11:30.133
but you will always learn
something more or something new

00:11:31.188 --> 00:11:35.355
and you will learn more overall
on bad days than good days.

00:11:38.322 --> 00:11:39.618
You will learn more about yourself,

00:11:39.618 --> 00:11:40.946
you'll learn more about
relationships, you'll

00:11:40.946 --> 00:11:42.449
learn about life and principles and it'll

00:11:42.449 --> 00:11:44.199
build your character.

00:11:45.757 --> 00:11:47.384
If you're a person who wants to let's say

00:11:47.384 --> 00:11:51.467
improve on your character
of patience, let's say,

00:11:52.341 --> 00:11:55.510
don't complain when
you're waiting in a line.

00:11:55.510 --> 00:11:57.564
You ain't going to grow in patience

00:11:57.564 --> 00:11:59.475
until you're put in a place to wait.

00:11:59.475 --> 00:12:03.228
It's like you go into a gym and, you know,

00:12:03.228 --> 00:12:04.978
you walking through the front doors

00:12:04.978 --> 00:12:07.210
and you know you tell
your wife or your husband

00:12:07.210 --> 00:12:08.636
I'm going to the gym.

00:12:08.636 --> 00:12:10.708
You go into the gym and
you come in three feet

00:12:10.708 --> 00:12:14.685
and you do a u-turn and you
ride out, I went to the gym.

00:12:14.685 --> 00:12:15.811
Ain't getting nothing.

00:12:15.811 --> 00:12:17.233
You got to go in and
what are you going to do?

00:12:17.233 --> 00:12:18.736
You're going to pick up the
weights and you exercise

00:12:18.736 --> 00:12:21.946
the muscles that you want to build.

00:12:21.946 --> 00:12:23.874
I stand before you without arms and legs,

00:12:23.874 --> 00:12:28.041
but a very strong man because
of the bad days in my life.

00:12:29.075 --> 00:12:30.658
You know how it is.

00:12:31.618 --> 00:12:33.527
If you didn't go what you've gone through,

00:12:33.527 --> 00:12:36.389
you wouldn't be who you are today.

00:12:36.389 --> 00:12:38.502
And I'm not belittling
your pain and don't worry,

00:12:38.502 --> 00:12:41.265
I've seen pain in my life,
and I've seen it not only

00:12:41.265 --> 00:12:43.521
in my live, but people's
lives and people say

00:12:43.521 --> 00:12:45.166
well at least I have no arms and legs

00:12:45.166 --> 00:12:46.526
and then what am I'm supposed to say?

00:12:46.526 --> 00:12:48.720
At least I'm not a
African orphan who's dying

00:12:48.720 --> 00:12:52.053
at four years old and I met that person.

00:12:54.047 --> 00:12:55.755
What about the 10-year-old
girl that was bought

00:12:55.755 --> 00:12:59.246
for 700 US dollars in Mamba
and kidnapped as a sex slave,

00:12:59.246 --> 00:13:01.891
to have 350 clients before the age of 13,

00:13:01.891 --> 00:13:03.655
pregnant at 12, put the baby under the bed

00:13:03.655 --> 00:13:07.109
while she works on top
abandoned by her family.

00:13:07.109 --> 00:13:09.750
After she pays her debt of 700 US dollars

00:13:09.750 --> 00:13:12.493
after three years with
her child she leaves

00:13:12.493 --> 00:13:15.155
on the streets of Mamba
hoping for a new life.

00:13:15.155 --> 00:13:17.006
No family, no job, no food.

00:13:17.006 --> 00:13:18.673
Her baby needs food.

00:13:19.607 --> 00:13:21.210
She gets raped, beaten up on the street.

00:13:21.210 --> 00:13:23.318
She comes back to the
only way that she knows

00:13:23.318 --> 00:13:24.484
how to make money.

00:13:24.484 --> 00:13:26.613
She goes back to the brothels.

00:13:26.613 --> 00:13:28.872
She gets pregnant at 15 the second time

00:13:28.872 --> 00:13:31.531
and then that child dies
and then at 20 years old

00:13:31.531 --> 00:13:36.268
she comes up to me, yes,
I have met this woman.

00:13:36.268 --> 00:13:37.661
She comes up crying and she
says "Nick, I just found

00:13:37.661 --> 00:13:39.244
I've got HIV AIDS."

00:13:44.366 --> 00:13:47.699
And I got fired from being a prostitute.

00:13:49.566 --> 00:13:51.566
What do you say to that?

00:13:53.670 --> 00:13:56.978
You may have arms and
legs, but unless you know

00:13:56.978 --> 00:13:59.970
three things, number
one, who are you and what

00:13:59.970 --> 00:14:02.950
your value is, number
two, what is your purpose

00:14:02.950 --> 00:14:05.554
here in life and number
three, what is your destiny

00:14:05.554 --> 00:14:07.387
when you're done here.

00:14:10.088 --> 00:14:11.766
If you don't know the
answers of any of those

00:14:11.766 --> 00:14:14.778
three questions, you're
more disabled than I.

00:14:14.778 --> 00:14:17.031
- So my quick thoughts are
I think it's generally good

00:14:17.031 --> 00:14:19.393
to try to avoid having bad days

00:14:19.393 --> 00:14:21.175
or bad moments, especially when

00:14:21.175 --> 00:14:24.310
they are happening frequently.

00:14:24.310 --> 00:14:25.992
I think anybody can have a bad day.

00:14:25.992 --> 00:14:28.292
And I think in general, you
can use some of the strategies

00:14:28.292 --> 00:14:30.161
in this video to help
you take those bad days

00:14:30.161 --> 00:14:31.909
and just chunk those into bad moments,

00:14:31.909 --> 00:14:34.509
so it doesn't bleed into the entire day

00:14:34.509 --> 00:14:36.460
or the next day, but one thing that I try

00:14:36.460 --> 00:14:38.451
to pay particular attention
to is if I'm feeling

00:14:38.451 --> 00:14:42.022
like this for multiple days in a row.

00:14:42.022 --> 00:14:44.157
If that's happening consistently,

00:14:44.157 --> 00:14:45.699
then I know something needs to change.

00:14:45.699 --> 00:14:47.327
If I'm getting up and
I'm looking in the mirror

00:14:47.327 --> 00:14:49.724
and I'm not happy for
multiple days in a row,

00:14:49.724 --> 00:14:51.390
or I'm looking at my
schedule of all the things

00:14:51.390 --> 00:14:53.567
I need to do and I'm not excited by it

00:14:53.567 --> 00:14:55.454
and I'm not motivated by it,
then I know that's something

00:14:55.454 --> 00:14:56.713
that needs to change.

00:14:56.713 --> 00:14:59.254
And that's not to say that
every moment is amazing

00:14:59.254 --> 00:15:01.955
and I look forward to every single thing

00:15:01.955 --> 00:15:03.685
that I'm ever going to do on my life.

00:15:03.685 --> 00:15:05.284
There's a lot of crap that comes

00:15:05.284 --> 00:15:06.733
with running a business, a lot of things

00:15:06.733 --> 00:15:08.643
that are not so good, a
lot of things that can

00:15:08.643 --> 00:15:11.219
get you down, but on the
surface, like on the whole,

00:15:11.219 --> 00:15:13.821
you should feel like the work you're doing

00:15:13.821 --> 00:15:15.893
is meaningful, it matters, you're growing,

00:15:15.893 --> 00:15:18.372
you're having a contribution
and you're excited

00:15:18.372 --> 00:15:19.531
about the work that you're doing,

00:15:19.531 --> 00:15:22.557
because if you're not,
you're not going to continue.

00:15:22.557 --> 00:15:24.706
It's just going to fade away.

00:15:24.706 --> 00:15:26.156
Your business won't have
success if you don't

00:15:26.156 --> 00:15:27.799
have the passion for it.

00:15:27.799 --> 00:15:29.773
So one, I think it's okay.

00:15:29.773 --> 00:15:31.495
I think it's okay to switch gears.

00:15:31.495 --> 00:15:32.960
I think it takes actually a lot of courage

00:15:32.960 --> 00:15:34.365
to switch gears.

00:15:34.365 --> 00:15:35.357
I think it takes a lot of courage

00:15:35.357 --> 00:15:38.144
to start off on some path that you thought

00:15:38.144 --> 00:15:39.891
you would enjoy and
then as you get into it,

00:15:39.891 --> 00:15:43.155
you realize, huh, this
isn't actually for me,

00:15:43.155 --> 00:15:45.499
but I'm going to keep on
this path that is not for me

00:15:45.499 --> 00:15:48.424
because I already invested
all of this time and money

00:15:48.424 --> 00:15:50.491
and effort into it, or I've already told

00:15:50.491 --> 00:15:52.488
my friends and family
that I'm going to do this

00:15:52.488 --> 00:15:55.820
and it would look really
bad if I stopped now.

00:15:55.820 --> 00:15:57.544
Those are the wrong reasons to do it.

00:15:57.544 --> 00:15:58.926
Just because you put a ton of energy

00:15:58.926 --> 00:16:00.326
into something, that doesn't mean

00:16:00.326 --> 00:16:01.323
you should keep doing it.

00:16:01.323 --> 00:16:02.786
Just because you're
worried about looking bad

00:16:02.786 --> 00:16:04.228
in front of somebody, it doesn't mean

00:16:04.228 --> 00:16:05.733
you should keep doing it.

00:16:05.733 --> 00:16:07.050
Take that thing that you no longer like

00:16:07.050 --> 00:16:09.473
and if you can sell it,
if you can get rid of it,

00:16:09.473 --> 00:16:11.113
if you can give it to somebody else, great

00:16:11.113 --> 00:16:13.780
and if not, dump it and
move on to something else.

00:16:13.780 --> 00:16:17.722
I have left more projects,
I've left more YouTube series

00:16:17.722 --> 00:16:21.555
than a lot of people
even ever dare to create.

00:16:22.389 --> 00:16:23.492
And it's part of the process.

00:16:23.492 --> 00:16:26.962
As you grow, as you evolve,
as you become a higher

00:16:26.962 --> 00:16:29.547
version of yourself, as
other interests come in,

00:16:29.547 --> 00:16:32.978
your business and the work
that you do can stay stagnant.

00:16:32.978 --> 00:16:34.684
You need to change the work that you do

00:16:34.684 --> 00:16:37.957
as you grow and evolve as a human being

00:16:37.957 --> 00:16:40.274
and so I find it super
valuable and super helpful

00:16:40.274 --> 00:16:43.241
that if I'm ever feeling
down for any consistent

00:16:43.241 --> 00:16:46.017
period of time, to look
at the work that I'm doing

00:16:46.017 --> 00:16:50.184
and evaluate it and say is that
still worth actually doing?

00:16:51.284 --> 00:16:52.767
Is that still worth my time.

00:16:52.767 --> 00:16:54.392
If I'm not motivated to
go out and do something

00:16:54.392 --> 00:16:56.610
and that's consistent,
then I need to find a way

00:16:56.610 --> 00:16:59.590
to get rid of it and move
on and go do something

00:16:59.590 --> 00:17:01.867
else that does ignite me,
that does get me excited,

00:17:01.867 --> 00:17:05.603
because that is where the
magic is going to happen,

00:17:05.603 --> 00:17:06.606
for me and for you.

00:17:06.606 --> 00:17:10.060
The more you are feeling
in the zone, in the moment,

00:17:10.060 --> 00:17:12.028
amazed at the work that you're doing,

00:17:12.028 --> 00:17:15.360
creative, impactful,
the more you're there,

00:17:15.360 --> 00:17:18.146
that is where the magic is going to happen

00:17:18.146 --> 00:17:20.155
for your business, for your life,

00:17:20.155 --> 00:17:22.305
so try to stay there as much as possible

00:17:22.305 --> 00:17:24.543
and eliminate the things that are causing

00:17:24.543 --> 00:17:26.395
these bad things for you.

00:17:26.395 --> 00:17:27.899
So thank you guys so much
for watching this edition

00:17:27.899 --> 00:17:28.929
of Believe Life.

00:17:28.929 --> 00:17:31.123
I made it because Prya asked me too,

00:17:31.123 --> 00:17:32.693
so if there's a topic
you'd like me to cover

00:17:32.693 --> 00:17:34.319
in the next edition of Believe Life,

00:17:34.319 --> 00:17:36.714
leave your requests in the comment below

00:17:36.714 --> 00:17:38.070
and we'll see what we can do.

00:17:38.070 --> 00:17:39.276
I'm also curious, what do you guys do

00:17:39.276 --> 00:17:40.290
when you have a bad day?

00:17:40.290 --> 00:17:41.935
What's your solution to get out of it?

00:17:41.935 --> 00:17:43.520
What are some of the
strategies and tactics

00:17:43.520 --> 00:17:45.859
that you use to bring yourself back up,

00:17:45.859 --> 00:17:48.680
whether that's a mindset
thing, a scheduling thing.

00:17:48.680 --> 00:17:50.306
What do you do to get out of a bad day?

00:17:50.306 --> 00:17:51.992
Leave it in the comments below.

00:17:51.992 --> 00:17:53.719
I'm curious and I think
you'll also be able

00:17:53.719 --> 00:17:56.663
to help others going
through similar problems.

00:17:56.663 --> 00:17:59.019
Finally, I want to give a quick
shout out to Atul Pathria.

00:17:59.019 --> 00:18:01.138
Atul, thank you so much
for creating that artwork

00:18:01.138 --> 00:18:03.576
about my book, Your One Word.

00:18:03.576 --> 00:18:05.299
I really appreciate the
love, time and energy

00:18:05.299 --> 00:18:08.452
that went into and just
wanted to say thank you.

00:18:08.452 --> 00:18:09.526
So thank you guys again for watching.

00:18:09.526 --> 00:18:10.845
I believe in you.

00:18:10.845 --> 00:18:12.897
I hope you continue to believe in yourself

00:18:12.897 --> 00:18:14.913
and whatever your one word is.

00:18:14.913 --> 00:18:17.330
Much love, I'll see you soon.

00:18:18.205 --> 00:18:20.343
(sonic boom)

